d Achilles is an independent standing in for the Democratic side."]}, "overview": "Senator Jim Risch seeks another term in one of the nation's most Republican-leaning states, where the partisan baseline favors his party by roughly eighteen points. He has raised over $3.3 million and holds a large cash advantage over independent challenger Todd Achilles, who has raised under $700,000 and says he would not caucus with either party.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the contest Safe or Solid for Republicans, and prediction markets give Risch roughly a 93 to 96 percent chance of winning. Polling is sparse and mixed in quality, but the most recent surveys show Risch well ahead. The race appears settled on fundamentals, with the main open question being the size of the final margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -10.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0421, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0262, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0261, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0098, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1557, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0384, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0175, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0222, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0056, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0107, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0089, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.009, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0086, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0152, "margin": -14.0}]}